## 1. Entry Points

Two Owner-facing commands. Nothing else reaches the company.

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `/goal` | Set, update, or extend a mission |
| `/hot-fix` | Emergency fix independent of the active goal |

`/ceo`, `/cto`, `/cqo`, `/coo`, `/cdo`, `/ops`, `/hiring` are not slash commands.
Internal routing uses agent/skill wiring only.

---

## 2. Think Before Acting

Don't assume. Don't hide confusion.

- State assumptions before implementing. If uncertain, ask.
- If multiple approaches exist, name them — don't pick silently.
- Minimum change that solves the problem. No speculative scope.
- If something is unclear, stop. Name what is unclear. Ask.

For hot-fix: smallest correct patch only. Do not "improve" adjacent code.
For goal: define verifiable success criteria before CEO routes to CXX.

